+# Required C0 integration after the contract patch
+
+This patch is deliberately a contract proposal, not a claim that applying the
+contract alone closes T1. C0 must complete every item below before either T1
+source/composition RED can become GREEN.
+
+1. Add a project reference from the WinUI app to this contract project.
+2. Implement `IVerifiedModelDownloadCoordinator` in
+   `Features/ModelImport/ModelDownload/ModelDownloadCoordinator.cs` using an
+   owned resumable transport. Construct observed evidence from the received
+   bytes and response identity, compare it to the requested catalog entry,
+   atomically publish only an exact verified match, and issue one inspection
+   request only after publication. Retirement, cancellation, stale generation,
+   duplicate completion, and late completion must publish and navigate zero times.
+3. Make `ModelDownloadCard.xaml.cs` select the compiled catalog entry by the
+   exact `OptimizationPreferenceBand`, pass its lifecycle token/generation to
+   the coordinator, and call `ModelImportPage.SubmitInputAsync` only through
+   `IVerifiedModelSubmissionBoundary` after rechecking `IsVerified` and exact
+   requested-artifact equality.
+4. Implement `IExactOptimizationResultConsumer` in Model Optimization storage.
+   The implementation must resolve Chat/export from the exact result plus
+   receipt, compare plan/configuration/source/hardware/output identity, manifest
+   digest, and byte length, reject runtime-only export, and never consult
+   `LastPublishedDirectory` or another ambient last-result field.
+5. Make `ModelOptimizationPage` retain the selected result and lifecycle
+   generation and call only that consumer for Chat/export.
+6. Add owner tests with controlled transports/tasks for all R4.1 download,
+   cancellation, exact-result, restart, substitution, and five-band catalog
+   cases. T1 then replaces its two composition REDs with ProjectReference-based
+   behavioral tests against those compiled owner seams.
+7. Extract the temporarily linked app families into referenceable projects:
+   ModelImport.Selection, ModelInspection.Contracts/Application,
+   ModelOptimization.Storage/Application, ModelHardwareCompatibility.Contracts,
+   and GgufRuntime.History/Services. Expose the worker environment policy from
+   its WorkerClient assembly. Replace each exact T1 link only after its owner
+   project preserves the shipping imports, generated inputs, constants,
+   analyzers, and references.
+
+Privacy/lifecycle rule: the public contracts carry opaque publication,
+destination, plan, configuration, digest, length, operation, and generation
+authority only. They carry no rooted path, provider payload, secret, ambient
+last-result state, or default lifecycle token.
